  - [0]: "Profile: Gal (age 6) communicates via AAC and strongly prefers interactive apps (drawing, music) over passive activities. Core interests: facts, drawing, music, and science—especially hands-on exploration (experiments, how things work, chemistry, weather), farm games, space topics (stars, moon, planets, rockets, astronauts), and programming (Code blocks, Games, Robots). Learning style: prefers hands-on, practical engagement and browses multiple options before committing to extended activities."
  - [1]: "Communication Style: Uses 'I'm thinking about' button to initiate guessing mode, preferring shorter, focused interactions with clear exit strategies. Typically looks down and to the side during communication—this is normal. When engagement seems uncertain, offer direct activity suggestions (e.g., 'Want to draw a rocket?') rather than waiting for menu selection. Frequently expresses tiredness via guessing mode. Responds positively to expanded activity options and specific, interest-based prompts."
  - [2]: "Safety & Concerns: (1) Expressed fear multiple times and seeks home/safety when scared (trigger unidentified—remain alert and reassuring). (2) Lost hat at school (confirmed April 9); shows persistence in communicating about it. (3) April 13: Expressed frustration and pressed 'Scissors' three times in succession—may indicate scissors-related incident at school or home. Monitor for clarification and continue offering reassurance and specific activities when frustrated."
  - [3]: "Session History (April 16-19): Gal has engaged in multiple focused sessions across drawing, space exploration, science experiments, interactive games, and multimedia learning. Consistent patterns: sustained engagement with hands-on activities (drawing app, bubbles game, sink-or-float experiments), strong interest in space topics (Mars, planets, rockets), willingness to provide details about personal activities, and excellent hand-eye coordination in reflex games. Note on YouTube browsing (April 19): Gal cycled between YouTube and Space buttons repeatedly, suggesting difficulty finding desired specific content. Recommendation: Offer direct activity suggestions (e.g., 'Want to watch a rocket launch video?') rather than abstract topic buttons when browsing appears uncertain."
  - [4]: "April 20 Session: Gal expressed interest in science videos (Kurzgesagt), then initiated guessing mode about 'something in the future.' Narrowed down to: Time → Future → asking about timeframe (later today, tomorrow, someday, next week). Pattern shows continued interest in science content and abstract thinking about future events."
  ↪ To append: action "add" at "/Student_Notes" with value. To update item: action "set" at "/Student_Notes/<index>".
